    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are looking at a robust offensive outlook today, led by **Trea Turner** (75.42) and **Kyle Schwarber** (71.37). **Trea Turner** earns top billing due to a high-floor matchup against Freeland; his leadoff role combined with a positive BvP historical edge (43 PA) makes him our most bankable asset for runs and stolen bases. **Kyle Schwarber** continues to thrive, receiving a boost from a favorable park factor and a platoon advantage that keeps his efficiency firmly in the elite tier. Notably, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.15) provides high-upside utility today, as the optimizer heavily weights his matchup against Leiter. His aggressive base-running profile against a slower delivery allows him to overcome an unfavorable #8 spot in the batting order, making him a critical weapon for our pursuit of category-scarcity in SB.\n\nRegarding tactical adjustments, the lineup is optimized around favorable SP xERAs, particularly with **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.93) enjoying a soft matchup against Kochanowicz. While the optimizer favors his 5.14 xERA matchup, we remain cautious about the overall depth of the bench due to significant external disruptions. We were forced to sit **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin** entirely due to rainouts, while **Christian Yelich** remains sidelined on the IL and **Zac Veen** is still grinding in Albuquerque. With no active bench assets available to pivot into the utility slot, the depth of our roster is currently compromised. While **Dillon Dingler** (47.13) and **Chase Meidroth** (51.75) represent our most marginal starts, they remain in the lineup to ensure we hit our daily game caps; should any late lineup scratches occur, we are thin on internal replacements to maintain our efficiency targets.",
